{
  "id": "ep075",
  "duration": 44.182,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.018,
      "text": "The Moon's brightest rocks are too young to exist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Back side of the Moon AS16-3021.jpg",
        "credit": "Apollo 16 astronauts",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_side_of_the_Moon_AS16-3021.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.018,
      "end": 8.288,
      "text": "Apollo missions found bright rocks called anorthosite that form the lunar highlands.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "John W. Young on the Moon.jpg",
        "credit": "Charlie Duke",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_W._Young_on_the_Moon.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.033,
          "end": 5.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 5.367,
          "end": 8.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 8.288,
      "end": 12.983,
      "text": "Experts thought these rocks floated to the surface of a global magma ocean.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA01478 Interior of Callisto.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA01478_Interior_of_Callisto.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 8.3,
          "end": 10.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 10.667,
          "end": 13.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.983,
      "end": 19.578,
      "text": "This coarse-grained rock is 90 percent plagioclase feldspar, which is less dense than liquid magma.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lunar anorthosite descartes highlands (36131355931).jpg",
        "credit": "the paleobear from Lontananza, Loreto, Peru",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lunar_anorthosite_descartes_highlands_(36131355931).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.0,
          "end": 19.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.578,
      "end": 27.973,
      "text": "But in 2011, researchers dated lunar Sample 60025 to only 4.36 billion years old.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "LUNAR SAMPLES - NARA - 17470453.jpg",
        "credit": "Martin Brown",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LUNAR_SAMPLES_-_NARA_-_17470453.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.567,
          "end": 22.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 22.867,
          "end": 27.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.973,
      "end": 32.298,
      "text": "This age is far too young for a crust formed during the Moon\u2019s birth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Moon- Lunar Prospecting With Chandra (2003-moon - moon illustration).tiff",
        "credit": "Optical: Robert Gendler; X-ray: NASA/CXC/SAO/J.Drake et al.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Moon-_Lunar_Prospecting_With_Chandra_(2003-moon_-_moon_illustration).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.967,
          "end": 30.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 30.8,
          "end": 32.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.298,
      "end": 37.443,
      "text": "Now scientists think the crust formed slowly through many volcanic eruptions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA18821-LunarGrailMission-OceanusProcellarum-Rifts-Closeup-20141001.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Colorado School of Mines/MIT/JPL/GSFC",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA18821-LunarGrailMission-OceanusProcellarum-Rifts-Closeup-20141001.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 32.3,
          "end": 37.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.443,
      "end": 43.832,
      "text": "New theories are rewriting lunar history to explain why the Moon's brightest rocks are too young to exist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Back side of the Moon AS16-3021.jpg",
        "credit": "Apollo 16 astronauts",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_side_of_the_Moon_AS16-3021.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.433,
          "end": 44.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
